## E3-SPC-v1 Symmetry-Plane Cantilever: half (z in [0,0.5]) of the 2 x 1 x 1 cantilever.
## Domain x in [0,2], y in [0,1], z in [0,0.5]; corner at the origin; cut plane z = 0.5.
## Structured HEX8 mesh, h = 1/24: 48 x 24 x 12 = 13,824 elements, 15,925 nodes.
## Sets: block_1 (all elements), ns_fix (x = 0 face), ns_load (edge x = 2, y = 0), ss_sym (faces on z = 0.5).
## Written for this trial from the frozen specification; the selection idiom follows the candidate Example 7 journal.
reset
#{len = 2.0}
#{ht  = 1.0}
#{wd  = 0.5}
#{esize = 0.0416667}
## --- geometry: half brick with its corner at the origin ---
create brick x {len} y {ht} z {wd}
move volume 1 x {len/2.0} y {ht/2.0} z {wd/2.0}
## --- structured (mapped) hex mesh 48 x 24 x 12 ---
volume 1 scheme map
volume 1 size {esize}
mesh volume 1
block 1 volume 1
block 1 name 'block_1'
block 1 element type HEX8
## --- fixed support: every node on the x = 0 face ---
nodeset 1 add node in surface with x_coord < {esize/2.0}
nodeset 1 name 'ns_fix'
## --- line load: every node on the edge x = len, y = 0 (spans z in [0, wd]) ---
nodeset 2 add node with x_coord > {len - esize/2.0} and with y_coord < {esize/2.0}
nodeset 2 name 'ns_load'
## --- symmetry (cut) plane: element faces on the surface z = wd ---
sideset 1 add surface with z_coord > {wd - esize/2.0}
sideset 1 name 'ss_sym'
export mesh "mesh.exo" dimension 3 overwrite
